---
layout: layouts/base.njk
desc: "Sarthak Bichhawa, Sr. Data & Applied Scientist at Microsoft Azure Storage. Applied AI and data platforms for incident response, customer health, and revenue attribution."
---

<header class="home-hero wrap">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Applied AI & data platforms · {{ facts.identity.org }} {{ facts.identity.team }}</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title">I make complex<br />systems <em>dependable.</em></h1>
    <p class="hero-intro">{{ facts.summary.hero }}</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#work" data-goatcounter-click="hero-work">Explore selected work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      <a class="text-link" href="{{ facts.resume.file }}" data-goatcounter-click="hero-resume-pdf">Résumé (PDF) <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-person">
    <img src="/assets/sarthak.jpg" alt="Sarthak Bichhawa" width="112" height="112" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
    <div>
      <p class="person-role">{{ facts.identity.title }}</p>
      <p class="person-context">{{ facts.identity.org }} · {{ facts.identity.location }}<br />Previously Walmart Labs</p>
      <a href="{{ facts.identity.linkedin }}" class="person-link" data-goatcounter-click="hero-linkedin">LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap">
  <ol class="home-outcomes" aria-label="Selected outcomes">
    {%- for id in facts.homepage.receipts %}
    {%- for r in facts.receipts %}{% if r.id == id %}
    <li><a href="{{ r.anchor }}"><span class="outcome-value">{{ r.value }}</span><span class="outcome-label">{{ r.label }}</span></a></li>
    {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
</div>

<section class="home-section wrap" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-heading">
  <div class="home-section-head">
    <h2 id="work-heading">Selected work</h2>
    <a href="/case/" class="text-link">All six case studies <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <article class="featured-case" aria-labelledby="featured-title">
    <div class="featured-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / Applied AI · In production</p>
      <h3 id="featured-title"><a href="/case/incident-agent/">From an incident alert to an evidence-backed answer.</a></h3>
      <p>An agent that tests competing hypotheses against live telemetry and produces a cited investigation brief.</p>
      <dl class="featured-ownership">
        <div><dt>My role</dt><dd>Design & implementation lead</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Key decision</dt><dd>Own the planner / executor loop</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <a class="case-link" href="/case/incident-agent/">Read the case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <figure class="featured-system">
      <figcaption class="eyebrow">An investigation</figcaption>
      <ol class="investigation-flow">
        <li><span class="flow-step">01</span><strong>Incident signals</strong><span>Telemetry + deployment state</span></li>
        <li><span class="flow-step">02</span><strong>Planner</strong><span>Competing hypotheses</span></li>
        <li><span class="flow-step">03</span><strong>Executor + tools</strong><span>Test against live evidence</span></li>
        <li><span class="flow-step">04</span><strong>Cited brief</strong><span>Confidence + query references</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="system-example"><strong>The decision that mattered</strong>A recent deployment looked responsible. The agent rejected that theory after checking the telemetry. <a href="/case/incident-agent/#trace">Explore the production replay <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
    </figure>
    <details class="featured-decision" id="decisions">
      <summary>Explore the engineering decision <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
      <div>
        <h4>Own the loop. Make every conclusion traceable.</h4>
        <p>I replaced the initial framework with a planner / executor loop to control tracing, retries, and context compaction. The trade-off: more orchestration code to maintain. A golden-set evaluation harness gates changes, and the final brief links claims to supporting queries.</p>
        <a href="/case/incident-agent/#decision" class="case-link">Architecture, evaluation, and lessons <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </details>
  </article>
  <div class="supporting-cases">
    <article aria-labelledby="revenue-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / Revenue systems</p>
      <h3 id="revenue-title"><a href="/case/revenue-attribution/">Making the numbers trustworthy.</a></h3>
      <p>I traced a silent attribution failure through 20+ components, drove six months of backfills, and redesigned the engine.</p>
      <p class="supporting-result">{{ facts.receipts[0].value }} in attribution recovered · &lt;1% variance vs Finance</p>
      <a href="/case/revenue-attribution/" class="case-link">Read the recovery <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
    <article aria-labelledby="health-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / Customer intelligence</p>
      <h3 id="health-title"><a href="/case/customer-health-agent/">Answers at the speed of a question.</a></h3>
      <p>I built an agent that turns plain-English questions into governed telemetry queries and review-ready narratives across 13 metric domains.</p>
      <p class="supporting-result">{{ facts.receipts[3].value }} for executive-review preparation</p>
      <a href="/case/customer-health-agent/" class="case-link">Explore the agent <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section wrap" id="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
  <div class="leadership-story">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Experience & leadership</p><h2 id="experience-heading">Build the system.<br />Bring the team.</h2></div>
    <div class="leadership-copy">
      <p>At Microsoft, I led a 4-team cross-org severity-2 response during the attribution recovery and aligned 8+ engineering and support teams around one customer-health program.</p>
      <p>Previously at Walmart Labs, I led 4 data scientists and 2 interns to productionize an item-level placement workflow.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/resume/" data-goatcounter-click="exp-resume-page">Full experience & résumé <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ol class="career-strip" aria-label="Career history">
    {% for role in facts.record %}
    <li><a href="/resume/#{{ role.id }}"><strong>{{ role.company }}</strong><span>{{ role.dates }}</span></a></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="home-section wrap home-writing" id="writing" aria-labelledby="writing-heading">
  <div class="home-section-head"><h2 id="writing-heading">Notes from production</h2><a href="/writing/" class="text-link">All writing <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  <ul class="posts">
    {% for w in facts.writing %}{% if w.url %}
    <li><a class="post-row" href="{{ w.url }}"><span class="post-date">{{ w.date | humanDate }}</span><span class="post-title">{{ w.title }}</span><span class="post-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="home-contact" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="contact-intro">
      <div><h2 id="contact-heading">Let’s build something dependable.</h2><p>Open to senior opportunities in applied AI and ML leadership.</p></div>
      <a href="mailto:{{ facts.identity.email }}" class="btn btn-primary" data-goatcounter-click="contact-email">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="contact-links"><a href="mailto:{{ facts.identity.email }}">{{ facts.identity.email }}</a><a href="{{ facts.identity.linkedin }}">LinkedIn</a><a href="{{ facts.identity.github }}">GitHub</a><a href="{{ facts.resume.file }}">Résumé (PDF)</a></div>
    <details class="disclosure">
      <summary>Plain-text summary, for your notes</summary>
      <div class="disclosure-body">
        <pre id="ats-summary">{{ facts.summary.ats }}
Site: {{ facts.meta.site_url }} · Résumé: {{ facts.meta.site_url }}{{ facts.resume.file }} · LinkedIn: {{ facts.identity.linkedin }} · Email: {{ facts.identity.email }}</pre>
        <button class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm copy-btn" type="button" data-goatcounter-click="contact-copy-summary">Copy</button>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
